                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Introduction[/h1]\n\n[i]A-Gents[/i] is a pixelated shooting game reminiscent of [i]Metal Slug[/i]. At the time I write this, you have the choice of playing one of two characters, Emma or Shean, who play the same. There isn’t too much of a story to the game, though each level has their own objective that offers some bit of a story if you’re interested. The game currently only has two episodes with five levels each but more are promised to come.\n\n[h1]Gameplay[/h1]\nYou can play the game with either a game controller or your keyboard and mouse. You can also play alone or with a friend locally. The game is pretty simple, you walk around and shoot down enemies and objects while clearing mission objectives and making it to the end of a level. There are a variety of guns to be used, or you can use a knife. You also have grenades which I found extremely useful as well dynamite to do heavy duty damage. A noted feature is that you can aim your gun 360 degrees, apparently before this update you could only aim in four directions though I haven’t played it that way.\n\n[h1]Graphics/Audio[/h1]\nThe game is fully pixelated so don’t expect too much in the graphics department. You can choose from two outfit choices for your character.  Like the choice of characters, this is solely cosmetic and their tiny pixels make it hard to see the clothes. However, I did like the retro feel of the graphics, while nothing fancy they still look good with nice colors and great locations. The music is also decent though not too memorable. It’s some basic rough sounding combat music so the tunes do fit the stages while you run around shooting baddies.  \n\n\n[h1]Pros[/h1]\n+ Great retro feel.\n+ A variety of weapons to choose from.\n+ Great to play with a friend.\n+ Three levels of difficulty.\n+ Each level gets increasingly longer adding new challenges.\n+ Steam achievements and trading cards.\n\n[h1]Cons[/h1]\n\n- Though you can play solo, it’s harder and not as enjoyable as playing with someone else.\n- Currently the price does not match the amount of content the game offers.\n\n[h1]Final Thoughts[/h1]\nI hope to see more from [i]A-Gents[/i], I enjoyed playing this game and have hopes that it will keep getting better since the developers do interact with the community. I hope the project is completed and recommend this game.  If you’re unsure about investing quite yet then keep an eye out for further updates to the game. I feel that when all the episodes are released that it will be even more fun.\n\n\n[b]Rating:[/b] 8.5/10\n\nThis review was submitted for [url=http://steamcommunity.com/groups/elitegives]Elite Giveaways[/url], check us out for more reviews ranging from Indie games to AAA games to F2P games.",
